          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "Each point is one case. The cases run from the smallest corpus on the left to the largest on the right. The Sonnet line stays above the Haiku line at all eight points, so its answer was the longer one in every case, by 1.5 to 2.6 times."
          },
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "Both lines fall to the right: an answer takes a smaller share of a bigger corpus. The two points at 1,091 lines are two questions about the same file."
          },
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "The eval calls this measure compression: the characters in the answer divided by the characters in the files the model read. Sonnet also wrote more output tokens, 628 against 404."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Sonnet pointed at the wrong line 8 times in 282, and Haiku never in 167",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "columns",
            "cols": [
              [
                {
                  "t": "stat",
                  "value": "0 of 167",
                  "label": "wrong line references from Haiku 5.5"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "t": "stat",
                  "value": "8 of 282",
                  "label": "wrong line references from Sonnet 5.5",
                  "sub": "5 of the 8 in one case"
                }
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "A line reference is a file and line number the model gives for a claim. It is wrong when the name the model mentions is not on that line. Five of the eight wrong ones are in the case `belt-validmode`, and the other three are in three different cases."
          },
          {
            "t": "p",
            "text": "A wrong line reference does not fail a run. The eval counts it apart from the pass."
          },
